Trim work painting - $33,862.00
Exterior Prep Scope of Work — 16640 Via Pacifica, Pacific Palisades, CA
Exterior Wood Window & Door Restoration — 16640 Via Pacifica, Pacific Palisades, CA
Scope of Work:
Restore all exterior wood-framed windows and exterior doors impacted by smoke and ember exposure.
1. Surface Preparation
Sand and clean all wood windows, trim, and door casings to remove soot residue, contaminants, and degraded coating
Spot prime any bare or exposed wood using a premium exterior-grade primer
Detail sanding performed by hand or fine tools to maintain original profile integrity
2. Finish Coating
Apply two full coats of high-performance exterior-grade paint or finish, brushed or sprayed based on accessibility and detail level
Use Sherwin-Williams Duration or equivalent premium product for superior protection and finish longevity
Match existing color and sheen unless otherwise directed by the client
3. Final Detailing
Inspect for uniformity and perform any necessary touch-ups
Re-caulk or seal joints around trim as needed
Mask and protect all adjacent finishes, glazing, and hardware throughout the process
Interior Repaint
$137,460.00
INTERIOR SCOPE – 16640 VIA PACIFICA, PACIFIC PALISADES
Project Overview:
On-site inspection revealed residual smoke odor in multiple areas of the home, particularly in upper-level rooms and along ceiling lines.
While the property has undergone partial cleaning, smoke damage remains evident in both scent and surface condition. Several rooms
feature high-end wallpaper (not yet replaced). Walls that previously had wallpaper will need to be prepped appropriately for new
installation. The home includes detailed architectural trim throughout, including crown molding, baseboards, door and window casings,
and other decorative wood elements — all of which will be fully refinished as part of the restoration process.
Scope of Work – Interior
1. Wallpaper Prep
Full prep for wallpaper installation in designated rooms (as marked by homeowner and wallpaper installer)
Prepare wall surfaces to a smooth, uniform substrate suitable for high-end paper
Apply Roman Pro-977 Ultra Prime or equivalent wallpaper primer, selected based on the type of wallpaper (e.g., silk, vinyl, grasscloth)
2. Interior Trim & Millwork Repaint
Prime and repaint all paint-grade interior trim and millwork, including:
Crown molding, baseboards, door/window casings, ceiling trims, panel moldings
All trim to be thoroughly sanded and caulked as needed, then spray-finished using Sherwin-Williams Duration Interior Enamel for a
smooth, factory-grade appearance
Color and sheen will match existing unless otherwise directed
3. Architectural Wood Elements Refinishing
