CAT SEL ACT DESCRIPTION
CALC QTY RESET REMOVE REPLACE TAX O&P TOTAL
Replacement of approximately 24 linear feet of full-height family room cabinetry is required due to pervasive smoke and ash contamination
resulting from a nearby fire event. While the cabinet surfaces may appear superficially intact, the cabinetry includes substantial voids, cavities, and
dead air space behind and within each unit — including between the cabinet backs and wall framing, as well as inside upper cabinets and lower
base structures.
Smoke particulates and odor-causing compounds are known to penetrate these enclosed areas, especially through seams, toe kicks, and the rear of
cabinet boxes. These areas are typically inaccessible for effective cleaning, and the absorptive materials (e.g., wood, adhesives, and backings) trap
odors long-term, even when sealed finishes are present on the exposed surfaces.
Due to the long-term risk of residual odor, off-gassing, and potential occupant health sensitivity, remediation is not a viable solution. Full removal
and replacement of the cabinetry is necessary to restore the room to pre-loss condition and ensure no residual odor remains. This scope includes
demolition, disposal, and installation of new cabinetry to match existing layout and finish.
