688. PLM STOP M Material Only Angle stop valve
2 2.00EA 0.00+ 12.48 = 2.37 5.48 32.81
The angle stop valve was replaced rather than reused due to the risk of failure associated with aging or previously disturbed plumbing components.
Reusing an old valve can result in leaks or malfunction, especially after being shut off and turned back on during repairs. Replacement ensures a
reliable seal, compliance with plumbing best practices, and minimizes future water damage risk.
689. PLM CAPC + Water line copper cap/plug - per cap
2 2.00EA 0.00+ 29.74 = 0.31 11.96 71.75
Copper plumbing caps have been installed on exposed angle stops to properly terminate water supply lines after fixture removal. This prevents
debris intrusion and potential water discharge, ensuring safety and compliance with industry standards during mitigation or repair phases. The caps
also allow for future reconnection of fixtures without additional plumbing modifications.
